BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Splat Space (Durham Hackerspace)
UID:event_314239114@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260523T035934Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260531T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260531T143000
SUMMARY:How Not to Be a Victim with Andy Foshee
DESCRIPTION:Splat Space - Durham's Hackerspace\nPresented by Triangle Mutu
 al Aid and hosted by Splat Space\n\nHow Not to Be a Victim: 300+ Tips to R
 esiliency is a comprehensive\, action-oriented program designed to shift i
 ndividuals from a passive state of worry to an active state of empowered c
 onfidence. This class provides over 300 practical\, actionable strategies 
 aimed at building mental\, physical\, and situational resilience\, ensurin
 g participants can handle unexpected adversity without relying on fear-bas
 ed tactics. Come by for a fast-paced talk on practical tips on how to go f
 rom victim to merely inconvenienced\, even on a budget. Please note nothin
 g will be for sale\, and there are no product endorsements\; this is stric
 tly an educational event. Handouts will be provided\; photos and videos ar
 e permitted.\nAbout the speaker: Andy Foshee is a volunteer and instructor
  with the Chatham Community Emergency Response Team (CERT)\n\nRSVP REQUIRE
 D
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/splatspace/events/314239114/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260412T023742Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260412T023742Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
